     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose looks wrong and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the maximum labeled dose.\n- Immediate-release metformin: max **2550 mg/day** (usually given as 850 mg three times daily)\n- Extended-release metformin: max **2000 mg/day**\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum IR dose)\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg twice daily with meals\n3. Something else, such as a different drug or dose\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm the original order with a clinical reason, and I'll enter it. If you confirm 1700 mg three times daily, I'll attach a note that it's above the labeled maximum and was confirmed by the prescriber."
      }
     ],
